Description: An optimization and benchmarking experiment derived from the
    'stringr' package. It provides the original route through installed
    'stringi', an independent backend returning ordinary R character vectors,
    and an independent backend returning 'ALTREP' character vectors through
    'charport'. It is not currently intended as a drop-in replacement for
    'stringr' or 'stringi'.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Copyright: This package is a fork of the 'stringr' package owned by Posit
    Software, PBC under the MIT License. It includes R and C++ code from the
    'stringi' package owned by Marek Gagolewski under the BSD 3-Clause License,
    and it bundles ICU4C source code and data owned by Unicode, Inc. and others
    under the Unicode License v3; the full notices are installed as COPYRIGHTS
    and icu/LICENSE. Benchmark measurements use sentences from the Tatoeba
    Project (<https://tatoeba.org>) under Creative Commons Attribution 2.0
    France; no Tatoeba data is included in this package.
